From: JD Lien <jd@jdlien.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:38:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ak820pro: codex's review of the RTC fixes (090378fd) --
 must-fix 1, a request during a running PCF write supersedes it: the writer
 re-plans from the board's clock before writing its time, or writes again
 (STOP held) if the time is already in, and the legacy set requests one
 whenever the writer is not idle; must-fix 2, the STOP recovery is bounded (6
 tries, 30 s), then deferred so the board may sleep, the PCF marked stale and
 maybe-stopped (neither its calendar nor its elapsed seconds trusted) until a
 write lands; must-fix 3, the stale wake's gain no longer counts the awake
 seconds since the wake twice, and a tick between its read and set is caught
 and redone; should-fix 4, a host's SKIP_PCF set leaves the PCF's staleness
 alone; should-fix 5, a correction voids a bracket in progress (no lead learnt
 from it); should-fix 6, the legacy set ends an older slew and restores the
 nominal period; pcf_pending_time removed (vestigial)

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Mm219BiSCsx6uwtXcZ7a9G
---
 keyboards/a_jazz/ak820pro/rtc/rtc.c          | 130 ++++++++++++++-----
 keyboards/a_jazz/ak820pro/rtc/rtc_pcf_sync.h |   7 +
 2 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

